{"seq":7,"slug":"eastern-philosophy","title":"东方哲学","stage":"DONE","category":"philosophy-logic","chapterCount":4,"docCount":16,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy","rating":{"composite":3.7,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.8,"coverage":3.25,"positioning":5,"strategic":3},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.1,"verdict":"neutral","uScore":2.25}},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"东方哲学-简介\">东方哲学 简介</h1><p>东方哲学是人类思想史上最悠久、最具原创性的传统之一，涵盖中国、印度及佛教文明数千年来对宇宙本体、人生意义、伦理秩序与解脱之道的探索。与西方哲学侧重逻辑分析和概念构建不同，东方哲学更强调直觉体悟、整体思维、关系性存在与实践智慧——这些恰恰是当代全球化与 AI 时代最稀缺的思想资源。</p>\n<p>本知识库按&quot;传统—传统—传统—对话&quot;的结构组织：先分别深入中国、印度、佛教三大思想体系，最后在东西方比较的视野中收束。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本-hub-的边界-与兄弟-hub-如何分工\">本 hub 的边界：与兄弟 hub 如何分工</h2><p>东方哲学与同目录下若干 hub 主题相邻但视角不同，明确边界可避免误入：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>想了解的问题</th>\n<th>来本 hub</th>\n<th>去这个兄弟 hub</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>儒释道印的思想体系本身</td>\n<td>✅ 东方哲学</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>苏格拉底到尼采的西方思想脉络</td>\n<td>仅在第四章作比较</td>\n<td><a href=\"../western-philosophy-history/\">09 西方哲学史</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>义务论/后果论/德性论的规范理论</td>\n<td>仅在第四章比较伦理</td>\n<td><a href=\"../ethics-foundations/\">03 伦理学基础</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&quot;存在&quot;&quot;共相&quot;&quot;因果&quot;等纯形而上学问题</td>\n<td>仅作东西方本体论对照</td>\n<td><a href=\"../metaphysics/\">10 形而上学</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>意识、心身、机器意识</td>\n<td>借唯识/吠檀多提供东方解答</td>\n<td><a href=\"../philosophy-of-mind/\">04 心灵哲学</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>上帝存在论证、神义论、宗教多元</td>\n<td>不涉及（本 hub 讲哲学而非宗教论证）</td>\n<td><a href=\"../philosophy-of-religion/\">13 宗教哲学</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>命题逻辑、一阶逻辑、模态逻辑</td>\n<td>仅讲印度因明的逻辑传统</td>\n<td><a href=\"../formal-logic/\">01 形式逻辑</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>海德格尔、现象学、存在主义</td>\n<td>仅作与禅/道的对话接点</td>\n<td><a href=\"../phenomenology-existentialism/\">14 现象学与存在主义</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>一句话：本 hub 负责<strong>东方诸传统的内部义理</strong>及其<strong>与西方的比较</strong>；纯西方主题、纯规范伦理、纯逻辑形式化各有专属 hub。</p>\n<h2 id=\"推荐学习路径-分人群\">推荐学习路径（分人群）</h2><p><strong>哲学初学者 / 想建立东方思维框架</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>先读第一章<a href=\"chinese-philosophy/confucianism\">儒家哲学</a>与<a href=\"chinese-philosophy/daoism\">道家哲学</a>，建立&quot;关系&quot;&quot;过程&quot;&quot;无为&quot;等基本直觉；</li>\n<li>进入第三章<a href=\"buddhist-philosophy/four-noble-truths\">四谛与缘起</a>，掌握佛教这一贯穿东亚的思想底座；</li>\n<li>最后读第四章<a href=\"east-west-dialogue/metaphysics-comparison\">本体论比较</a>收束全局。</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>已有西方哲学背景 / 想拓展跨文化视野</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>直接从第四章<a href=\"east-west-dialogue/comparative-methodology\">比较哲学方法论</a>入手，先建立比较的方法自觉（避免东方主义陷阱）；</li>\n<li>按你熟悉的西方议题反查东方对应：关心意识就读<a href=\"indian-philosophy/vedanta\">吠檀多</a>与<a href=\"buddhist-philosophy/yogacara\">唯识哲学</a>，关心逻辑就读<a href=\"indian-philosophy/indian-logic\">印度因明学</a>，关心伦理就读<a href=\"east-west-dialogue/ethics-comparison\">伦理观比较</a>；</li>\n<li>以第四章<a href=\"east-west-dialogue/modern-synthesis\">当代融合与前瞻</a>了解新儒学与京都学派的真实综合成果。</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>技术 / 知识工作者 / 关心实践应用</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><a href=\"buddhist-philosophy/zen-philosophy\">禅宗哲学</a>（极简、正念、当下觉知）→ <a href=\"chinese-philosophy/daoism\">道家哲学</a>（为道日损、少即是多）；</li>\n<li><a href=\"buddhist-philosophy/madhyamaka\">中观哲学</a>（破除认知偏见的治疗性方法）；</li>\n<li><a href=\"east-west-dialogue/modern-synthesis\">当代融合与前瞻</a>中的 AI 伦理与关系伦理章节。</li>\n</ol>\n<p>对单一传统有专门兴趣的读者，也可直接进入对应章节，每篇均自足成文。</p>\n<h2 id=\"前置知识\">前置知识</h2><ul>\n<li><strong>必备</strong>：能区分本体论、认识论、伦理学三大哲学分支；理解&quot;概念分析&quot;与&quot;直觉体悟&quot;两种进路的差别。</li>\n<li><strong>有帮助但非必需</strong>：西方哲学史的基本轮廓（柏拉图、亚里士多德、康德、海德格尔），便于读懂第四章的比较；佛教/印度术语的基本梵汉对照（各篇均有表格随文给出，无须预先掌握）。</li>\n<li><strong>不需要</strong>：任何宗教信仰背景——本 hub 把儒释道印当作<strong>哲学</strong>来读，关注其论证与洞见，而非信仰实践。</li>\n</ul>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"chinese-philosophy","title":"中国哲学传统","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/chinese-philosophy","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"confucianism","title":"儒家哲学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/chinese-philosophy/confucianism"},{"seq":2,"slug":"daoism","title":"道家哲学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/chinese-philosophy/daoism"},{"seq":3,"slug":"chinese-buddhism","title":"中国佛学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/chinese-philosophy/chinese-buddhism"},{"seq":4,"slug":"neo-confucianism","title":"宋明理学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/chinese-philosophy/neo-confucianism"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"indian-philosophy","title":"印度哲学传统","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/indian-philosophy","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"vedanta","title":"吠檀多哲学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/indian-philosophy/vedanta"},{"seq":2,"slug":"yoga-samkhya","title":"瑜伽与数论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/indian-philosophy/yoga-samkhya"},{"seq":3,"slug":"jainism-philosophy","title":"耆那教哲学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/indian-philosophy/jainism-philosophy"},{"seq":4,"slug":"indian-logic","title":"印度因明学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/indian-philosophy/indian-logic"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"buddhist-philosophy","title":"佛教哲学","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/buddhist-philosophy","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"four-noble-truths","title":"四谛与缘起","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/buddhist-philosophy/four-noble-truths"},{"seq":2,"slug":"madhyamaka","title":"中观哲学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/buddhist-philosophy/madhyamaka"},{"seq":3,"slug":"yogacara","title":"唯识哲学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/buddhist-philosophy/yogacara"},{"seq":4,"slug":"zen-philosophy","title":"禅宗哲学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/buddhist-philosophy/zen-philosophy"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"east-west-dialogue","title":"东西方哲学对话","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/east-west-dialogue","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"comparative-methodology","title":"比较哲学方法论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/east-west-dialogue/comparative-methodology"},{"seq":2,"slug":"metaphysics-comparison","title":"本体论比较","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/east-west-dialogue/metaphysics-comparison"},{"seq":3,"slug":"ethics-comparison","title":"伦理观比较","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/east-west-dialogue/ethics-comparison"},{"seq":4,"slug":"modern-synthesis","title":"当代融合与前瞻","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/eastern-philosophy/east-west-dialogue/modern-synthesis"}]}]}